# MagicSquare Python Code Style Rules

## Runtime and Style Baseline
- Python version: 3.13.13
- Style guide: PEP 8
- Maximum line length: 88

## Type Hints and Docstrings
- Type hints are required for all function parameters and return values.
- Public functions, methods, and classes must include Google-style docstrings.

## General Quality Rules
- Prefer explicit names over abbreviations.
- Keep functions small and focused on one responsibility.
- Avoid hidden side effects and implicit state mutations.
